course: dictionary
lesson: 1906
title: Colourless: no colour, pale, or dull
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Each hair of a polar bear's fur is colourless, and the skin underneath is black.» Colourless means having no colour at all. The second sentence says, «A polar bear's fur looks white, but each hair is actually colourless», so the fur looks white without being white. The word «actually» is a clue that something looks one way but is really another.
explain: Colourless can also mean pale and grey, as in «a colourless face». A face with no colour in it looks tired, ill or frightened. Read the words around it: a face is a person, so the word is describing how that person looks, not what they are made of.
explain: Colourless can mean dull and boring, as in «a colourless town», where nothing bright or interesting stands out. In science, a colourless liquid like water or a colourless gas like oxygen has no colour you can see. But colourless does not mean safe or invisible: some colourless gases are poisonous.
fact: Colourless means having no colour at all, like clear water or air.
fact: «Colourless» can also mean pale and grey, as in «a colourless face».
fact: «Colourless» can mean dull and boring, as in «a colourless town».
fact: Phrases you will meet in science are «colourless liquid», «colourless gas» and «colourless and odourless».
fact: Colourless is not the same as invisible or safe, because some colourless gases are poisonous.
exercise: «Each hair of a polar bear's fur is colourless, and the skin underneath is black.» What does colourless mean here? | Bright red | *Having no colour at all | Very shiny and gold | Painted in many colours
exercise: Why do scientists warn that a colourless gas is not always safe? | Colourless gases are always safe to breathe | Colourless means you cannot see it at all | Colourless gases are always heavy | *Some colourless gases are poisonous
exercise: «A colourless town» suggests a town that is what? | Bright and full of paint | Made of glass and very fragile | *Dull and boring, with nothing interesting
test: «Her face was colourless after the fright.» What does colourless mean here? | *Pale and grey | Bright red from running | Hidden under water | Painted in many colours
test: Which phrase is a science phrase? | *colourless liquid | painted face | colourful rainbow | loud whisper
exam: Mia says a colourless gas must be safe because you cannot see it. What is the best reply? | *Not so: some colourless gases are poisonous | Yes, because colourless means invisible | No, colourless gases are always sweet smelling | Yes, anything you cannot see is safe
